worktree: ../okay-wt-body
spec: specs/optics-outside.md (stage 7)

why: the consumer was found before the feature, as stage 4 established.
  okay-demo's `/login` and `/login/confirm` pick their fields out of the
  request body by string literal — `Chat.fieldOf(r.body, "email")` —
  which is the same shape stage 2 removed from `BoardTools`, and it
  carries a live defect: `fieldOf` answers `""` both for a MISSING
  field and for a body that is not JSON at all, so the two are
  indistinguishable. `/login` checks for the empty string and answers
  400; `/login/confirm` does not, and passes ("", "") into
  `Login.confirm`, so a malformed request is reported to the caller as
  **401 "wrong or expired code"**. The routes are covered only by
  `portTest`, which is Live-tagged and out of the default gate, so
  nothing would have caught it.

what: `Router.json[B]` declares the body's type. It decodes with
  `Schema[B]` before the handler runs, answers 400 with data when the
  body does not decode, and records the body's JSON Schema on the
  entry so `describe` carries it — which is what a renderer will need
  and what stage 2 already does for tools.

next: spec stage 7, Router.json, a pure test of the mechanism, the two
  ChatDemo routes, one Live assertion for the 400, docs
